# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 262-267 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, RUN 2, 2026-09-26): the bite — the borrower and the lender, the
# tithe money and the fodder, the greeting as interest (262); to the foreigner and not the brother, interest before and after, the blessing and the reward (263);
# the vow paired with the freewill offering, valuations and devotions, no exchange, the sin in you not in your offering (264); better not to vow, the three
# commandments of the lips, the court's warning, the list of 23:24's words (265); the laborer in the vineyard — while he gathers, grapes not figs, more than
# his wage (266); the standing grain — by hand, no sickle (267). Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(262, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"BITE NOT YOUR BROTHER" (23:20) — THIS IS THE BORROWER; THE LENDER WHENCE? LEVITICUS 25:36 "TAKE NO BITE OR INCREASE FROM HIM". The head row of piska 262 ({SP_(262, 1, "זה", "לוה")} "this is the borrower"; {SP_(262, 1, "מלוה", "מנין")} "the lender — whence?"): THE TWO PARTIES each under a verse — Deuteronomy the borrower (who pays the bite), Leviticus the lender; the frozen Leviticus 25 cell reused with the borrower\'s arm (the design\'s (a)); the design\'s DV23-03. Fresh.')
srow(262, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR SILVER" AND NOT OTHERS\' SILVER, "YOUR FOOD" AND NOT OTHERS\' FOOD — OR NOT TITHE MONEY, NOT ANIMAL FODDER? "THE BITE OF SILVER" INCLUDES TITHE MONEY, "THE BITE OF FOOD" INCLUDES FODDER; ONLY SILVER AND FOOD? "THE BITE OF ANYTHING THAT BITES". ({SP_(262, 2, "ולא", "כסף", "אחרים")} "and not others\' silver"; {SP_(262, 2, "לרבות", "כסף", "מעשר")} "to include tithe money"; {SP_(262, 2, "לרבות", "אכלי", "בהמה")} "to include animal fodder"; {SP_(262, 2, "מנין", "לרבות", "כל", "דבר")} "whence to include everything?"): the three nouns of 23:20 (silver, food, anything) each a widening of Leviticus 25:37\'s two — the class of the loan\'s object unbounded. Fresh.')
srow(262, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON: WHENCE THAT THE LENDER NOT SAY "GO AND ASK AFTER SO-AND-SO", OR "FIND OUT IF SO-AND-SO CAME"? "THE BITE OF ANYTHING THAT BITES". ({SP_(262, 3, "צא", "ושאל", "שלום", "פלוני")} "go and ask after So-and-so\'s welfare"): an errand is interest — Bava Metzia 5:10\'s verbal interest (the English\'s "cf."); the object\'s class reaches a favor. Fresh.')
srow(263, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO THE FOREIGNER YOU MAY BITE, TO YOUR BROTHER NOT" (23:21) — THE FIRST A POSITIVE COMMANDMENT, THE SECOND A NEGATIVE. The head row of piska 263 ({SP_(263, 1, "לנכרי", "תשיך", "מצות", "עשה")} "to the foreigner bite — a positive commandment"; {SP_(263, 1, "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "a negative commandment"): the foreigner\'s arm of the interest cell (the design\'s (a)) — a permission read as a command. Fresh.')
srow(263, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'RABBAN GAMLIEL: WHY "TO YOUR BROTHER YOU SHALL NOT BITE" WHEN 23:20 SAID IT? THERE IS INTEREST IN ADVANCE AND INTEREST AFTER: A GIFT SENT SO THAT HE WILL LEND — IN ADVANCE; REPAID, THEN A GIFT "FOR YOUR MONEY THAT LAY IDLE WITH ME" — AFTER. ({SP_(263, 2, "יש", "רבית", "מקדמת", "ויש", "רבית", "מאחרת")} "there is interest in advance and interest after"; {SP_(263, 2, "זה", "הוא", "רבית", "מקדמת")} "this is interest in advance"; {SP_(263, 2, "זה", "הוא", "רבית", "מאחרת")} "this is interest after"): Bava Metzia 5:10 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — the redundancy of the two verses the two clocks of the gift, before and after the loan. Fresh.')
srow(263, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"THAT THE LORD YOUR GOD MAY BLESS YOU IN ALL YOU PUT YOUR HAND TO" — SCRIPTURE FIXED HIM A BLESSING IN THE STRETCHING OF THE HAND. ({SP_(263, 3, "קבע", "לו", "הכתוב", "ברכה", "בשליחות", "יד")} "Scripture fixed him a blessing in the stretching of the hand"): the reward trope (64:2\'s, the English) — the blessing on the work. Fresh.')
srow(263, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"ON THE LAND YOU ARE COMING TO POSSESS" — AS REWARD FOR COMING YOU WILL POSSESS. ({SP_(263, 4, "בשכר", "שתבא", "תירש")} "as reward for coming you will possess"): 55:3\'s trope (the English) — the land formula\'s seat. Fresh.')
srow(264, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU VOW A VOW TO THE LORD" (23:22) — "VOW" SAID HERE AND SAID THERE (LEVITICUS 7:16): AS THERE THE VOW IS PAIRED WITH THE FREEWILL OFFERING, SO HERE; AS HERE "DELAY NOT TO PAY IT", SO THERE. The head row of piska 264 ({SP_(264, 1, "נאמר", "כאן", "נדר", "ונאמר", "להלן", "נדר")} "\'vow\' is said here and said there"; {SP_(264, 1, "נדר", "ונדבה")} "a vow and a freewill offering"; {SP_(264, 1, "לא", "תאחר", "לשלמו")} "delay not to pay it"): A VERBAL ANALOGY IN BOTH DIRECTIONS — the freewill offering under the delay\'s bar, the peace offering\'s vow under it; Numbers 30\'s vow daemon takes the CLOCK "delay not" (the design\'s DV23-04; Rosh Hashanah 1:1 the compile\'s answer sheet, not cited here). Fresh.')
srow(264, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" — THESE ARE VALUATIONS, DEVOTIONS AND CONSECRATIONS. ({SP_(264, 2, "אלו", "ערכים", "וחרמים", "והקדשות")} "these are valuations, devotions and consecrations"): Leviticus 27\'s three classes named as the vow\'s objects — the frozen unit\'s cells the callees (the design\'s (e)). Fresh.')
srow(264, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"DELAY NOT TO PAY IT" — IT AND NOT ITS EXCHANGE. ({SP_(264, 3, "הוא", "ולא", "חלופיו")} "it and not its exchanges"): Leviticus 27:10\'s substitution barred — the vowed beast itself. Fresh.')
srow(264, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR HE WILL SURELY SEEK IT OF YOU" — THESE ARE SIN OFFERINGS AND GUILT OFFERINGS. ({SP_(264, 4, "אלו", "חטאות", "ואשמות")} "these are sin offerings and guilt offerings"): the obligatory offerings under the delay\'s bar — the infinitive absolute "seek" (find 14\'s seven) the widening. Fresh.')
srow(264, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE LORD YOUR GOD" — THIS IS THE CONSECRATION FOR THE HOUSE\'S REPAIR. ({SP_(264, 5, "זה", "הקדש", "בדק", "הבית")} "this is the consecration for the House\'s repair"): the sanctuary\'s fund in. Fresh.')
srow(264, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"OF YOU" — THESE ARE GLEANINGS, THE FORGOTTEN SHEAF AND THE CORNER. ({SP_(264, 6, "זה", "לקט", "שכחה", "ופאה")} "gleanings, the forgotten sheaf and the corner"): the poor\'s dues (24:19-21 ahead, Leviticus 19:9 behind) counted among the delayed — the forgotten sheaf named in chapter 23 before its verse. Fresh.')
srow(264, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THERE SHALL BE SIN IN YOU" — IN YOU SIN, AND NOT IN YOUR OFFERING. ({SP_(264, 7, "בך", "חטא", "ולא", "בקרבנך", "חטא")} "in you sin and not in your offering"): the delayed offering still fit — the sin the vower\'s (find 7\'s formula at its second seat); the effect on the person, not the beast. Fresh.')
srow(265, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"BUT IF YOU REFRAIN FROM VOWING" (23:23) — R. MEIR: ECCLESIASTES 5:4 "BETTER NOT TO VOW THAN TO VOW AND NOT PAY" — BETTER THAN BOTH NOT TO VOW AT ALL; R. JUDAH: BETTER THAN BOTH TO VOW AND PAY. The head row of piska 265 ({SP_(265, 1, "טוב", "מזה", "ומזה", "שלא", "תדר", "כל", "עקר")} "better than both not to vow at all"; {SP_(265, 1, "נודר", "ומשלם")} "one who vows and pays"): the Writings\' receipt of 23:22-23 (Ecclesiastes 5:4-5 the verse\'s twin); the dispute on counsel, not on law — no sin either way (find 7\'s negative). Fresh.')
srow(265, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHAT YOUR LIPS UTTER" (23:24) — A POSITIVE COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(265, 2, "מצות", "עשה")} "a positive commandment"): 23:24 carries no head — its rows inside 265; the utterance the vow\'s form (Nedarim 1:1\'s handles the compile\'s parameter). Fresh.')
srow(265, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"KEEP" — A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(265, 3, "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "a negative commandment"): "keep" (shamar) read as a prohibition — the book\'s usage (4:2). Fresh.')
srow(265, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND DO" — A WARNING TO THE COURT TO COMPEL YOU. ({SP_(265, 4, "אזהרה", "לבית", "דין", "שיעשוך")} "a warning to the court to compel you"): THE COURT\'S ARM in the vow — the third verb the enforcement (the design\'s (f)). Fresh.')
srow(265, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AS YOU VOWED" — THIS IS A VOW. ({SP_(265, 5, "זה", "נדר")} "this is a vow"): the first of six words of 23:24 each given a class. Fresh.')
srow(265, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" — VALUATIONS, DEVOTIONS AND CONSECRATIONS. ({SP_(265, 6, "אלו", "ערכים", "וחרמים", "והקדשות")} "these are valuations, devotions and consecrations"): 264:2 repeated for 23:24. Fresh.')
srow(265, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"A FREEWILL OFFERING" — THIS IS THE FREEWILL OFFERING. ({SP_(265, 7, "זו", "נדבה")} "this is a freewill offering"): the pair of 264:1. Fresh.')
srow(265, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH YOU SPOKE" — THE CONSECRATION FOR THE HOUSE\'S REPAIR. ({SP_(265, 8, "זה", "הקדש", "בדק", "הבית")} "this is the consecration for the House\'s repair"): 264:5 repeated. Fresh.')
srow(265, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITH YOUR MOUTH" — THIS IS CHARITY. ({SP_(265, 9, "זו", "צדקה")} "this is charity"): the pledge to the poor a vow the court compels — the last of the six. Fresh.')
srow(266, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU COME INTO YOUR FELLOW\'S VINEYARD" (23:25) — AT ANY TIME? THE TEACHING SAYS "INTO YOUR VESSEL PUT NOT" — WHILE YOU PUT INTO THE OWNER\'S VESSELS. The head row of piska 266 ({SP_(266, 1, "יכול", "לעולם")} "might it be at any time?"; {SP_(266, 1, "בשעה", "שאתה", "נותן", "לתוך", "כליו", "של", "בעל")} "when you put into the vessels of the owner"): THE LABORER, not the passer-by — the verse\'s "you" the hired hand at his gathering; Onkelos writes "when you are hired" (23:25\'s row); the design\'s DV23-05, Bava Metzia 7 the compile\'s answer sheet. Fresh.')
srow(266, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR FELLOW" — EXCLUDING OTHERS; "YOUR FELLOW" — EXCLUDING THE MOST HIGH\'S. ({SP_(266, 2, "פרט", "לאחרים")} "excluding others"; {SP_(266, 2, "פרט", "לגבוה")} "excluding the Most High\'s"): the owner\'s class — an Israelite, not the sanctuary. Fresh.')
srow(266, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND EAT" — AND NOT SUCKING OUT. ({SP_(266, 3, "ולא", "ממצץ")} "and not sucking out"): eating, not pressing the juice — the Tosefta\'s row (the English). Fresh.')
srow(266, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"GRAPES" — AND NOT FIGS; HENCE: WORKING AT FIGS HE EATS NO GRAPES, AT GRAPES NO FIGS — BUT HE HOLDS BACK UNTIL HE REACHES THE FINE ONES AND EATS. ({SP_(266, 4, "ולא", "תאנים")} "and not figs"; {SP_(266, 4, "עד", "שמגיע", "למקום", "היפות", "ואוכל")} "until he reaches the place of the fine ones and eats"): Bava Metzia 7:4 the answer sheet\'s row (the English\'s "=") — the crop he works is the crop he eats. Fresh.')
srow(266, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELAZAR HISMA: WHENCE THAT A LABORER NOT EAT MORE THAN HIS WAGE? "AS YOUR SOUL"; THE SAGES: "YOUR FILL" — HE EATS MORE THAN HIS WAGE. ({SP_(266, 5, "שלא", "יאכל", "פועל", "יותר", "על", "שכרו")} "that a laborer not eat more than his wage"; {SP_(266, 5, "שאוכל", "פועל", "יותר", "על", "שכרו")} "that a laborer eats more than his wage"): THE MEASURE PARAMETER disputed — the wage a cap or no cap; the Tosefta\'s row. Fresh.')
srow(266, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"INTO YOUR VESSEL PUT NOT" — WHILE YOU PUT INTO THE OWNER\'S VESSELS. ({SP_(266, 6, "בשעה", "שאתה", "נותן", "לתוך", "כליו")} "when you put into his vessels"): 266:1\'s clause for itself — the time of eating the time of gathering. Fresh.')
srow(267, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU COME INTO YOUR FELLOW\'S STANDING GRAIN" (23:26) — AT ANY TIME? "SWING NO SICKLE" — WHILE YOU SWING THE SICKLE OVER THE OWNER\'S GRAIN. The head row of piska 267 ({SP_(267, 1, "יכול", "לעולם")} "might it be at any time?"; {SP_(267, 1, "בשעה", "שאתה", "מניף", "חרמש")} "when you swing the sickle"): the reaper as the vintager — the same shape on the grain. Fresh.')
srow(267, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"HIS FELLOW" — EXCLUDING OTHERS; "HIS FELLOW" — EXCLUDING THE MOST HIGH\'S. ({SP_(267, 2, "פרט", "לאחרים")} "excluding others"; {SP_(267, 2, "פרט", "לגבוה")} "excluding the Most High\'s"): 266:2 again; the export\'s lemma reads "his fellow" for the verse\'s "your fellow" (the printed text\'s variant, the English\'s note on "Babylonians"). Fresh.')
srow(267, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU MAY PLUCK EARS WITH YOUR HAND" — THAT YOU NOT REAP WITH A SICKLE. ({SP_(267, 3, "שלא", "תהא", "קוצר", "במגל")} "that you not reap with a sickle (magal)"): the hand the instrument — Onkelos\'s very noun (magla, 23:26\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(267, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"SWING NO SICKLE" — WHILE YOU SWING THE SICKLE OVER THE OWNER\'S GRAIN. ({SP_(267, 4, "על", "קמת", "בעל", "הבית")} "over the owner\'s standing grain"): 267:1\'s clause for itself — the chapter\'s last row; 268:1 opens on 24:1 (the edge clean, the ink\'s assert). Fresh.')
